BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature Booth: Geology\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260627T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260627T170000
UID:614f710203e7af83b9261eb429269e0f@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Visit the lobby of the Abe Martin Lodge anytime between 4pm an
 d 5pmpm to see fossiles\, geodes\, and other interesting rocks! Learn abou
 t the geologic processes found in Indiana&#39\;s bedrock and ask the natur
 alist your questions! If the weather is nice\, we may be on the front porc
 h instead.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Abe Martin Lodge (lobby)\, 1405 S.R. 46
  W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260627T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260627T223000
UID:df364aca7fa45d46d2c01e1fbbe651da@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike on the Salt Cre
 ek Trail! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to i
 nteresting views along the creek. Learn about June&#39\;s full moon this y
 ear\, the Strawberry Moon. The Salt Creek Trail is rated very easy\, but s
 hould be considered moderate in the dark. The trail has some minor slopes\
 , a short stretch of lawn\, and possible wet or icy spots depending on wea
 ther. Our route is&nbsp\; about 2 miles total and will take about an hour 
 to complete. Please do not bring pets on night hikes. Red flashlights are 
 preferred for night vision and can be loaned to hikers on request. Hike ca
 ncellation policy: Hikes will be cancelled if there is lightning\, tempera
 tures below 0 degrees Farenheit\, temperature indexes above 105 degrees Fa
 renheit\, or a wind advisory. If a hike is cancelled\, gatehouses will be 
 informed. The phone number for the North Gatehouse is 812-988-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Olympic Pool parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46
  W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
